# Provenance — charts/README.md § `SOURCE` is required, including when nothing was forked.
#
# ADR-010: "Their charts are a starting point, not a dependency. Where a chart is close, fork it into
# charts/ with the upstream commit recorded in a SOURCE file." Nothing was forked here, and
# `vendored: none` is an answer to "where did this come from" where a missing file is not.

vendored: none
upstream: https://github.com/cloudnative-pg/cloudnative-pg

# The upstream API this chart's template targets. ⚠ An API group/version, not a commit: nothing is
# vendored, so there is no upstream tree to pin. The same group charts/managed/postgres renders a
# Cluster into; this chart renders the ScheduledBackup that names one.
upstream-api: postgresql.cnpg.io/v1

# Reviewed against upstream sources at the tag the bundle pins — charts/bundle/cloudnative-pg,
# v1.30.0 — on this date. A tag rather than a SHA is a weaker claim and is labelled as one.
#
# ⚠ WHAT THIS REVIEW ESTABLISHED, because every one of these decided a line in the template or the
# reconciler, or ruled a design out:
#
#   * `api/v1/scheduledbackup_types.go` — ScheduledBackupSpec is {suspend, immediate, schedule,
#     cluster, backupOwnerReference, target, method, pluginConfiguration, online,
#     onlineConfiguration}. `schedule`: "The schedule does not follow the same format used in
#     Kubernetes CronJobs as it includes an additional seconds specifier" — so the API takes five
#     fields and the template prepends the sixth. `backupOwnerReference`: "none: no owner reference
#     … self: sets the Scheduled backup object as owner of the backup — cluster: set the cluster as
#     owner"; `self` is what makes the vault's teardown reach its recovery points. `method`:
#     barmanObjectStore, volumeSnapshot or plugin.
#
#   * `api/v1/scheduledbackup_funcs.go` — CreateBackup sets ObjectMeta {Name, Namespace} and calls
#     utils.InheritAnnotations with the operator's configuration; IT COPIES NO LABELS from the
#     ScheduledBackup onto the Backup. ADR-013's seven therefore never reach a recovery point, and a
#     join on cybercloud.io/resource-id finds none.
#
#   * `internal/controller/scheduledbackup_controller.go` — the controller labels each Backup it
#     creates with utils.ClusterLabelName = the cluster and utils.ParentScheduledBackupLabelName =
#     the ScheduledBackup's name, and marks the first one utils.ImmediateBackupLabelName. The schedule
#     is parsed with robfig/cron's `cron.Parse`. THAT LABEL IS THE JOIN: RecoveryVaults.RecoveryPointSelector
#     lists Backups by `cnpg.io/scheduled-backup=<name>`.
#
#   * `pkg/utils/labels_annotations.go` — ClusterLabelName "cnpg.io/cluster",
#     ParentScheduledBackupLabelName "cnpg.io/scheduled-backup", ImmediateBackupLabelName
#     "cnpg.io/immediateBackup"; BackupStartTimeAnnotationName / BackupEndTimeAnnotationName are
#     annotations, not status, and the reconciler reads status.startedAt/stoppedAt instead.
#
#   * `api/v1/backup_types.go` — BackupPhase: pending, started, running, finalizing, completed,
#     failed, walArchivingFailing, "invalid backup definition". BackupStatus carries phase,
#     startedAt, stoppedAt, error, backupId, backupName, method. `completed` is the one phase
#     RecoveryVaults.RecoveryPoint.IsCompleted accepts for a recover.
#
#   * `internal/controller/backup_controller.go` — the Backup reconciler sets NO labels of its own,
#     and its prerequisite check fails a Backup whose cluster has no spec.backup with "cannot proceed
#     with the backup as the cluster has no backup section", and one whose method is
#     barmanObjectStore against a cluster with no barmanObjectStore section with "no
#     barmanObjectStore section defined on target cluster". The vault refuses a server with
#     backup.enabled false for exactly this reason, before the operator has to.
#
#   * seaweedfs-csi-driver `pkg/driver/driver.go` at v1.4.20 — the controller capabilities are
#     CREATE_DELETE_VOLUME, SINGLE_NODE_MULTI_WRITER, EXPAND_VOLUME and (with the attacher)
#     PUBLISH_UNPUBLISH_VOLUME; NO CREATE_DELETE_SNAPSHOT, NO LIST_SNAPSHOTS. That is why this chart
#     renders no VolumeSnapshot for a file share and the brief's second protected type is owed:
#     conformance.yaml § owed, `file-shares-have-no-snapshot-story`.
#
# ⚠ WHAT WAS NOT REVIEWED, stated so nobody reads silence as coverage: the ScheduledBackup
# validating webhook's exact rules beyond "the schedule parses" — a schedule the five-field pattern
# admits and robfig/cron refuses (a day-of-month of 32, say) is refused by the operator at admission,
# after the caller was told 202, and the operation reports the API server's message. And
# `bootstrap.recovery.backup.name`'s behaviour when the Backup's status.barmanObjectStore is absent —
# the recover handler refuses a point that is not `completed`, which is the case that would reach it.
reviewed: 2026-09-18

# ⚠ The mutating webhook defaults `target` and `online` on a ScheduledBackup, so RecoveryVaults.Matches
# is containment over the three fields the vault owns rather than equality.
upstream-webhook: mutating, defaults target and online
